["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>The goose year decides which birds are in front of you: big local families in September, migrants in October, wary survivors in December.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A goose year, month by month. January: winter flocks on open water. February: pairs firm up and move north. March: nesting starts mid month. April: eggs, 25 to 28 days. May: goslings hatch and walk off. June: moult, cannot fly. July: young grow fast. August: young fly at 6 to 9 weeks. September: big local birds, early season. October: migrants arrive. November: lakes freeze and birds drop down to open valley water. December: cold, feed in the afternoon.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A Canada goose year in BC</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"34\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"34\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jan</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Winter flocks, open</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">water</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"75\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"75\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"99\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feb</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Pairs firm up, move</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">north</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"116\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"116\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mar</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nesting starts mid</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">month</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"157\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"157\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apr</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Eggs: 25 to 28 days</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"198\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"198\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">May</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Goslings hatch, walk</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">off</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"239\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"239\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"263\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jun</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"263\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Moult: cannot fly</text><rect x=\"208\" y=\"34\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"208\" y=\"34\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jul</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Young grow fast</text><rect x=\"208\" y=\"75\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"208\" y=\"75\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"99\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aug</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Young fly at 6 to 9</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">weeks</text><rect x=\"208\" y=\"116\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"208\" y=\"116\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Big local birds;</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">early season</text><rect x=\"208\" y=\"157\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"208\" y=\"157\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Migrants arrive</text><rect x=\"208\" y=\"198\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"208\" y=\"198\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Lakes freeze, birds</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">drop down</text><rect x=\"208\" y=\"239\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"208\" y=\"239\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"263\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dec</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Cold: feed in the</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"271\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">afternoon</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange: nesting. Blue: moult. Dark: fall season</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Nest in spring, moult in summer, move in fall <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>October and November change the most (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>Month by month, January to December.</li><li>The nest, the moult and the young.</li><li>What changes in October and November.</li><li>Which goose is in BC in which month.</li><li>Season dates are only quoted from the <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds\">Rule Book</a>. No new dates here.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Timeline chart, September 2026 to March 2027, of Canada and cackling goose seasons, 10 a day, 99 percent. District 3, Kamloops: 8 to 20 September, 1 October to 23 December, 1 to 10 March. District 8, Okanagan: 20 September to 28 November, 20 December to 5 January, 21 February to 10 March. District 2, Mission: 5 to 15 September, 10 October to 22 November, 19 December to 10 January, 10 February to 10 March. Gaps are closed.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Canada and cackling geese, 10 a day (99%)</text>\n  <line x1=\"100.0\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"100.0\" y2=\"246\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/>\n  <text x=\"120.7\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep</text>\n  <line x1=\"141.4\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"141.4\" y2=\"246\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/>\n  <text x=\"162.1\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct</text>\n  <line x1=\"182.9\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"182.9\" y2=\"246\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/>\n  <text x=\"203.6\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov</text>\n  <line x1=\"224.3\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"224.3\" y2=\"246\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/>\n  <text x=\"245.0\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dec</text>\n  <line x1=\"265.7\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"265.7\" y2=\"246\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/>\n  <text x=\"286.4\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jan</text>\n  <line x1=\"307.1\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"307.1\" y2=\"246\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/>\n  <text x=\"327.9\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feb</text>\n  <line x1=\"348.6\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"348.6\" y2=\"246\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/>\n  <text x=\"369.3\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mar</text>\n  <text x=\"92\" y=\"87.66666666666667\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">District 3</text>\n  <text x=\"92\" y=\"103.66666666666667\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Kamloops</text>\n  <rect x=\"109.7\" y=\"74.7\" width=\"18.0\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"141.4\" y=\"74.7\" width=\"113.6\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"348.6\" y=\"74.7\" width=\"13.4\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"92\" y=\"151.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">District 8</text>\n  <text x=\"92\" y=\"167.0\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Okanagan</text>\n  <rect x=\"126.2\" y=\"138.0\" width=\"95.3\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"249.7\" y=\"138.0\" width=\"22.7\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"336.7\" y=\"138.0\" width=\"25.2\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <text x=\"92\" y=\"214.33333333333334\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">District 2</text>\n  <text x=\"92\" y=\"230.33333333333334\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Mission</text>\n  <rect x=\"105.5\" y=\"201.3\" width=\"15.2\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"153.5\" y=\"201.3\" width=\"59.8\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"248.3\" y=\"201.3\" width=\"30.7\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"320.5\" y=\"201.3\" width=\"41.5\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gaps are closed. District 3: closed 21 to 30 Sept</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Winter flocks hold open water and fields <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Spring moves start as early as February <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the months in full</summary><ul><li>Winter: geese feed a few hours in early morning and late afternoon in fields, then rest on water (80%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li><li>Some populations start north in February; northern breeders arrive late April or early May (75 to 80%).</li><li>Pairs form in a goose's second year; spring is when pairs settle on territories <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>In temperate areas nesting can start as early as mid March <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Late season days quoted from the Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>: District 3 (Kamloops), Canada and cackling geese 1 to 10 March. District 8 (Okanagan), 21 February to 10 March in a year that is not a leap year. District 2 (Mission), 10 February to 10 March 2027.</li><li>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Number <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Eggs</td><td>4 to 7, sometimes 2 to 11</td></tr><tr><td>Sitting (incubation)</td><td>25 to 28 days, hen only</td></tr><tr><td>Leave the nest</td><td>1 to 2 days after hatch</td></tr><tr><td>First flight</td><td>6 to 9 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Survive to fly</td><td>About half</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>The hen sits; the gander guards <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Families walk several kilometres in a few days after hatch <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the nest in full</summary><ul><li>The hen picks a slightly raised dry spot near water with a good view and builds a shallow bowl lined with down (80%, Audubon).</li><li>Most geese do not nest until they are 2 or 3 years old (80%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li><li>In BC Canada geese nest mostly below 500 m (85%, BC Breeding Bird Atlas via the quick lesson).</li><li>Okanagan towns addle eggs within 14 days of incubation to control introduced geese (85%, Regional District of Okanagan Similkameen). That is a permit program, not hunting.</li><li>Spring is a time to stay away from nests. No goose season runs in April or May in any BC district (95%, my reading of the Rule Book tables).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A goose with no flight feathers and five long feathers lying below it: all flight feathers drop at once. Flightless for 4 to 6 weeks, June into August, 70 percent. Non breeding geese fly north to moult, late May to June, 80 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Summer moult: grounded for weeks</text><g transform=\"translate(150 150) scale(2)\"><ellipse rx=\"22\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -6 L36 0 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-4\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -5 L51 -3 L45 -1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -6 L0 -16 L8 -6Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/></g><path d=\"M110 210 l6 40 l4 -40Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" transform=\"rotate(-20 113 230)\"/><path d=\"M126 210 l6 40 l4 -40Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" transform=\"rotate(-10 129 230)\"/><path d=\"M142 210 l6 40 l4 -40Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" transform=\"rotate(0 145 230)\"/><path d=\"M158 210 l6 40 l4 -40Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" transform=\"rotate(10 161 230)\"/><path d=\"M174 210 l6 40 l4 -40Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" transform=\"rotate(20 177 230)\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">All flight feathers drop at once</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"50\" width=\"140\" height=\"110\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320.0\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Flightless</text><text x=\"320.0\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4 to 6 weeks</text><text x=\"320.0\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">June into August</text><text x=\"320.0\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(70%)</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"170\" width=\"140\" height=\"110\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320.0\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Non breeders</text><text x=\"320.0\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">fly north to</text><text x=\"320.0\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">moult: late May</text><text x=\"320.0\" y=\"247\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">to June (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>All flight feathers drop at once: 4 to 6 weeks flightless <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Non breeders fly north to moult in late May and June <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: moult in full</summary><ul><li>Hinterland Who's Who gives a 4 to 5 week flightless moult <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>; a city naturalist guide gives 4 to 6 weeks, about the same time the goslings cannot fly <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Timing: usually June into August <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Non breeding geese make a moult migration, late May to early June (80%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li><li>Goslings fly at 6 to 9 weeks, the biggest races later (80%, Audubon).</li><li>You will find moulted flight feathers on lake shores in summer. Good sign for next fall (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-08\">Chapter 8</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 325\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Season bar chart: Region 3 geese: open dates. Snow and Ross&#x27;s geese: Sept 8 to Dec 23. White fronted geese: Sept 8 to Dec 23. Canada and cackling geese: 3 periods: Sept 8 to Sept 20, Oct 1 to Dec 23, Mar 1 to Mar 10. Closed Sept 21 to Sept 30.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"325\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Region 3 geese: open dates</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"47\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Page 34. MUs 3-12 to 3-20, 3-26 to 3-44.</text>\n<text x=\"38.6\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep</text>\n<text x=\"92.7\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct</text>\n<text x=\"146.8\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov</text>\n<text x=\"200.9\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dec</text>\n<text x=\"255.9\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jan</text>\n<text x=\"308.2\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feb</text>\n<text x=\"360.5\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mar</text>\n<line x1=\"12.0\" y1=\"91\" x2=\"12.0\" y2=\"315\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n<line x1=\"65.2\" y1=\"91\" x2=\"65.2\" y2=\"315\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n<line x1=\"120.2\" y1=\"91\" x2=\"120.2\" y2=\"315\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n<line x1=\"173.4\" y1=\"91\" x2=\"173.4\" y2=\"315\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n<line x1=\"228.4\" y1=\"91\" x2=\"228.4\" y2=\"315\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n<line x1=\"283.4\" y1=\"91\" x2=\"283.4\" y2=\"315\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n<line x1=\"333.0\" y1=\"91\" x2=\"333.0\" y2=\"315\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n<line x1=\"388.0\" y1=\"91\" x2=\"388.0\" y2=\"315\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Snow and Ross&#x27;s geese</text>\n<rect x=\"24.4\" y=\"113\" width=\"189.8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<text x=\"220.2\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Sept 8 to Dec 23</text>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">White fronted geese</text>\n<rect x=\"24.4\" y=\"169\" width=\"189.8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<text x=\"220.2\" y=\"185\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Sept 8 to Dec 23</text>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"219\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Canada and cackling geese: 3 periods</text>\n<rect x=\"24.4\" y=\"225\" width=\"23.1\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<rect x=\"65.2\" y=\"225\" width=\"149.0\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<rect x=\"333.0\" y=\"225\" width=\"17.7\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"263\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Sept 8 to Sept 20, Oct 1 to Dec 23, Mar 1 to</text>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"281\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Mar 10</text>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"303\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Closed Sept 21 to Sept 30</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>September geese are mostly local, big and in family groups (Tip, 65%).</li><li>District 3 Canada geese close 21 to 30 September <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: September in full</summary><ul><li>Early season dates (99%, Rule Book): District 3, 8 to 20 September. District 2, 5 to 15 September 2026. District 8 opens 20 September.</li><li>Young birds fly by late summer and look like adults by fall <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Families are still feeding on hay, pasture and the first grain stubble near their home water (Tip, 65%).</li><li>Hunter lore: early season birds have not been shot at yet and decoy best (Tip).</li><li>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two panels. October: migrant flocks join the local geese, a Tip; cackling geese reach wintering areas October to November, 75 percent; snow geese peak on the Fraser delta, 80 percent. November: high lakes freeze first, 60 percent; birds crowd onto open valley water, 75 percent; after weeks of shooting the birds are warier, a Tip. Season dates differ by district: check the Rule Book before every trip, 99 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What changes in October and November</text><rect x=\"15\" y=\"40\" width=\"180\" height=\"200\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"205\" y=\"40\" width=\"180\" height=\"200\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"15\" y=\"40\" width=\"180\" height=\"30\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"61\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">October</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"40\" width=\"180\" height=\"30\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"295\" y=\"61\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">November</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Migrant flocks join</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the locals (Tip)</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cacklers reach winter</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">areas Oct to Nov (75%)</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Snow geese peak on</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the Fraser delta (80%)</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">High lakes freeze first</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(60%)</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Birds crowd open</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">valley water (75%)</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Weeks of shooting:</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">warier birds (Tip)</text><rect x=\"15\" y=\"250\" width=\"370\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rule: dates differ by district. Check the</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"287\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rule Book before every trip (99%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Migrants and cacklers join the locals <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>High lakes freeze and birds crowd the valley water <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: October and November in full</summary><ul><li>Northern geese leave their breeding areas late August to September and reach wintering areas in October or November (75%, Ducks Unlimited). Some linger in the north until early October (80%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li><li>Snow geese reach the Fraser delta by early October and peak mid October to mid December (80%, <a href=\"#/s/migration\">How animals move</a>).</li><li>Fall migration is well under way by late September and mostly over by late November, when Interior lakes freeze (75%, Ducks Unlimited via the migration lesson).</li><li>High plateau lakes freeze first; birds then crowd onto open valley water and the coast (60%, my reading in the migration lesson).</li><li>After weeks of shooting, flocks flare sooner and land farther out (Tip, 65%). Change the spread. See <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-04\">Chapter 4</a>.</li><li>Heffley Creek in October: District 3 Canada and cackling geese open 1 October to 23 December, 10 a day <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Mission: District 2 opens 10 October 2026 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart, September to April, of when each goose is in BC. Local Canada geese: all year, 85 percent. Migrant Canada geese: September to November, a Tip. Cackling geese: passing in fall and again in spring, 75 percent. Snow geese on the Fraser delta: October to mid December, then back mid March to April, 80 percent; most shift to the Skagit in Washington late December to February. White fronted geese: passing in early fall and spring, a Tip, 60 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Which goose, which month (BC)</text><text x=\"156.0\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep</text><text x=\"188.0\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct</text><text x=\"220.0\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov</text><text x=\"252.0\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dec</text><text x=\"284.0\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jan</text><text x=\"316.0\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feb</text><text x=\"348.0\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mar</text><text x=\"380.0\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apr</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Canada, local</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"70\" width=\"256\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"400\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text><text x=\"132\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Canada, migrants</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"106\" width=\"96\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"400\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text><text x=\"132\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Cackling</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"142\" width=\"96\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9c7c5c\"/><rect x=\"332\" y=\"142\" width=\"64\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9c7c5c\"/><text x=\"400\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text><text x=\"132\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Snow, Fraser</text><rect x=\"172\" y=\"178\" width=\"112.0\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#7aa6c9\"/><rect x=\"348.0\" y=\"178\" width=\"48.0\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#7aa6c9\"/><text x=\"400\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text><text x=\"132\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Snow, Skagit WA</text><rect x=\"261.6\" y=\"214\" width=\"86.4\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#c8d9e8\"/><text x=\"400\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text><text x=\"132\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">White fronted</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"250\" width=\"64\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#b07d4f\"/><rect x=\"364\" y=\"250\" width=\"32\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#b07d4f\"/><text x=\"400\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Snow dates 80%. Migrant and white front bars: Tip</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Local Canada geese: all year <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Snow geese: Fraser delta October to April, Skagit in deep winter <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 260\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Snow geese calendar. They reach the Fraser delta by early October, peak mid October to mid December, mostly shift to the Skagit in Washington late December to February, return mid March to mid April, then fly home to Wrangel Island, Russia, in April.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Snow geese and the Fraser delta</text>\n<line x1=\"100\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"111\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text>\n<line x1=\"124\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"124\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"135\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">F</text>\n<line x1=\"146\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"146\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"157\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">M</text>\n<line x1=\"170\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"181\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text>\n<line x1=\"194\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"194\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"205\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">M</text>\n<line x1=\"218\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"218\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"229\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text>\n<line x1=\"241\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"241\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"252\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text>\n<line x1=\"266\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"266\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"276\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text>\n<line x1=\"290\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"301\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">S</text>\n<line x1=\"313\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"313\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"324\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">O</text>\n<line x1=\"337\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"337\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"348\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">N</text>\n<line x1=\"361\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"361\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"372\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">D</text>\n<text x=\"92\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Fraser delta</text>\n<rect x=\"313\" y=\"59\" width=\"71\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<rect x=\"157\" y=\"59\" width=\"24\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<text x=\"92\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Peak</text>\n<rect x=\"324\" y=\"103\" width=\"48\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"92\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Skagit, WA</text>\n<rect x=\"380\" y=\"147\" width=\"6\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<rect x=\"100\" y=\"147\" width=\"45\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">April: home to Wrangel Island, Russia (80%)</text>\n</svg></figure><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the details and the gaps</summary><ul><li>Snow geese: Fraser delta by early October, peak mid October to mid December, most shift to the Skagit in Washington late December to February, return mid March to mid April, then fly to Wrangel Island in April <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Cackling geese pass BC on the way to the Willamette and lower Columbia valleys <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>; exact Interior dates: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li><li>White fronted geese: passing flocks in early fall and spring, a Tip <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>. No BC count found.</li><li>Migrant Canada geese in the Interior: from the first hard frosts of October (Tip, 65%, quick lesson).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 252\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a cursor moves from September 2026 to March 2027 over the Region 2 duck and Canada goose seasons. Canada geese open 5 to 15 September. Ducks and geese open 10 October. Ge