tainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>District 2 Canada geese close 23 November to 18 December <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: December in full</summary><ul><li>Below about minus 9°C (15°F) at sunrise, a big wintering flock usually skipped its morning flight; on the coldest days only a few birds fed (80%, Raveling 1972).</li><li>In bitter cold geese roost through the morning and feed when it is warmest (65%, Ducks Unlimited goose guide).</li><li>Snow on fields: geese feed where wind or cattle bared the ground (Tip).</li><li>District 3 closes 23 December; District 2 reopens 19 December 2026 to 10 January 2027; District 8 reopens 20 December to 5 January (99%, Rule Book).</li><li>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Memory rhymes (made for this app)</div><ul><li>\"March they nest, June they rest, fall they fly, winter they try.\"</li><li>\"September: big and local. October: new and vocal. December: few and fickle.\"</li></ul></aside><ul><li>Number trick: <strong>28, 6, 9</strong>. About 28 days sitting, about 6 weeks flightless, young fly by 9 weeks <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Old hand's rule (tradition, opinion)</div><p>First hard frost, look up. Hunters across the north watch for the first cold snap to bring new birds. A Tip, not a measured trigger.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Hinterland Who's Who, Audubon, Ducks Unlimited, Raveling 1972, city naturalist moult guide, Rule Book. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.hww.ca/en/wildlife/birds/canada-goose.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hinterland Who's Who</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https:/